module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.citation_verified_against_a_rendering_that_destroyed_its_scope

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data citation_verified_against_a_rendering_that_destroyed_its_scope: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "citation_verified_against_a_rendering_that_destroyed_its_scope" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**A CITATION CHECKED AGAINST A RENDERING OF ITS SOURCE IS CHECKED AGAINST AN ARTEFACT THAT NO LONGER CARRIES WHAT MAKES THE CITATION TRUE OR FALSE.** A verbatim quotation is not only a string; it is a string WITH A SCOPE -- the element that authored it and the heading that governs it. Rendering to text preserves the string and destroys both. So a reader working from the rendering can confirm the wording perfectly and still be wrong about whose fact it is, and the confirmation feels like exactly the verification that was asked for. ",

    "TWO SPECIMENS, OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS, ONE MECHANISM (2026-09-08, gunbc colo census, sessions silent-heron-303 / keen-newt-324 / bright-swift-678 and this one). FUSION -- THE STRING IS INVENTED FROM REAL PARTS. A spec strip authored as two sibling list items, `<li><strong>35kW+</strong> Cab Density Air</li>` and `<li><strong>100kW+</strong> Cab Density Liq</li>`, renders as two adjacent lines and was captured as one comma'd English sentence that appears nowhere in the bytes. FOUR INDEPENDENT INSTANCES ON FOUR FACILITIES OF ONE OPERATOR, produced by three different readers, which is what establishes it as a property of the page template rather than of any reader. LOCALITY -- THE STRING IS REAL AND BELONGS TO SOMEONE ELSE. `12 kW of 2x 208V/50A A+B redundant power in a 42U configuration` reproduced in the bytes EXACTLY, on the page of the facility being modelled, and sat under a block headed `Limited Time: Chicago-Area Facility`. Real figure, published price, wrong metro. It was the densest cabinet in the census and it was another region's. ",

    "**THE SECOND SPECIMEN IS THE LOAD-BEARING ONE BECAUSE IT DEFEATS THE REPAIR THE FIRST ONE MOTIVATES.** The fusion class was closed by a rule saying: confirm the wording OCCURS IN THE RAW BYTES. That rule passes cleanly on the Chicago figure. A string-occurrence test cannot fail on a correctly-transcribed string attached to the wrong subject, which is precisely the error the citation discipline exists to prevent -- so the first repair, honestly applied, admits the worse of the two errors. A verification that is sound for one member of a class and silent for another member of the same class is not a partial repair; it is a repair that certifies the residue. ",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE: whenever a quotation has been confirmed by finding the string, ask what ABOVE and AROUND the string in the source decides which subject it belongs to, and whether the artefact you searched still contained that.** If the answer is a rendering, the check established transcription and nothing about attribution. ",

    "THE REPAIR IS AT MARKUP GRAIN AND ONLY AT MARKUP GRAIN, which is the finding worth keeping because it is decidable. Element boundaries settle fusion: one `<li>` containing the whole wording is an authored cell; two `<li>`s joined by a comma is invention -- and tag-stripped text cannot express the difference, so the intuitive fix of stripping tags before matching destroys the evidence for the first specimen while fixing the third problem below. Byte order settles locality: the nearest heading or banner preceding the match is the figure's scope, and a promotion block, another product line or another metro named there disqualifies the row for this facility. A row's citation should record the boundary it was read from, not merely the sentence. ",

    "A THIRD ARM FOUND WHILE REPAIRING THE SECOND, RECORDED BECAUSE IT FAILS IN THE REASSURING DIRECTION. Matching the wording literally against the RAW bytes returns no match for a real citation whenever the numeral is emphasized -- `<li><strong>10kW+</strong> Cab Density Air</li>` contains no contiguous `10kW+ Cab Density Air` -- and emphasizing the numeral is how these tables are built. So the raw-byte rule, applied to the WORDING question, wrongly withdraws true rows, while the tag-stripped rule, applied to the FUSION question, wrongly admits false ones. THE TWO QUESTIONS NEED TWO ARTEFACTS: match the wording against tag-stripped text, decide fusion and scope against the markup. A single artefact cannot answer both, and choosing either one alone produces a confident wrong answer in a different direction. ",

    "AND THE SUMMARIZING READER IS WRONG IN BOTH DIRECTIONS ON THE SAME PAGE, so tightening the prompt is not the repair: the same instrument that invented a sentence also DENIED, when asked for verbatim text only, that the word `cabinet` occurs on a page whose own section heading is `High-Density Cabinets`. A negative answer from a summarizer is not evidence of absence any more than a positive one is evidence of presence. This is [[absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked]] arriving through a reader rather than through an instrument's aim, and the shared repair is the same: a positive control in the same invocation over the same artefact -- grep something the page certainly contains -- so that an empty result is separated from a failed fetch and a refused pattern. Both of those were also observed here: the fetch tool's rate-limit page returns HTTP 429 as a body that reads as a document, and a bounded-repeat pattern was refused with exit 2 whose empty stdout is indistinguishable from exit 1's. ",

    "THE COST OF NOT HAVING THIS ROW, measured on the census that produced it: verbatim auditing REDUCED the readable-density population rather than growing it -- one metro from four rows to two, one corridor from two to one of twenty-eight facilities -- and every withdrawal was a row that had passed a plausibility read. A capture that is fluent, correctly formatted and about the right facility is the artefact this class produces, so the population it inflates is exactly the population an author is least motivated to re-check. ",

    "Distinct from [[positional_citation]], where the citation names a POSITION that decays as the source is edited; here the citation names the right text and the wrong OWNER, and it decays at capture time rather than over time. Distinct from [[stable_citation_mutable_referent]], where the referent moved after a correct read; here the referent never moved and was never correctly read. Distinct from [[type_name_field_carries_rendered_value]], which is a rendering stored where a structured value belonged -- the loss there is in what the corpus CARRIES, here in what the corpus was CHECKED AGAINST. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, and the mitigation was a human re-reading page bytes, which is the weakest form the rung has. Nothing prevented the authoring, nothing flagged it, and no consumer could have distinguished the wrong figure from a right one -- while the Chicago row stood it was SILENT WRONGNESS, which is not a rung but the state below the ladder that DESIGN section 5 forbids outright. The class is filed at mitigatable because it is now contained: the carrier's typed arms make an unread density recordable as `DensityUnread` rather than absent, and the withdrawn rows were withdrawn rather than downgraded. That containment is real and it is entirely retrospective. ",

    "CEILING: structurally impossible, for BOTH halves, and the derivation is what makes it that rather than a ratchet. The two invalid states are a wording that SPANS TWO ELEMENTS and a wording SCOPED BY A HEADING NAMING ANOTHER SUBJECT. Both are decidable given the captured bytes -- element containment is a tree question and enclosing-heading is a byte-order question, neither requiring a predicate to be lifted to proof -- and both have NO CONSTRUCTOR once the wording can only be minted as a projection of one captured element together with its enclosing heading path. The residual is the external boundary and it is not a rung: whether the captured bytes are that page, today, is upstream reality, observed at a declared boundary and never fabricated. So the ceiling is impossibility of MISATTRIBUTION WITHIN A CAPTURE, not impossibility of a stale capture. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: a captured-source carrier whose mint takes the captured bytes and an element identity within them and YIELDS the wording, so that `claim_wording` cannot be inhabited by a hand-typed String at all, carrying the enclosing heading path beside it and joining that path against the facility the row is about. It must be SUFFICIENT FOR: no author can write a wording spanning two elements, and no author can write a wording whose enclosing heading names a different facility, promotion or metro. A carrier that merely STORES the bytes beside the wording does not discharge this -- the two would still be independently writable and a single author would satisfy both in one edit, which is the artifact-shaped trigger this ledger warns about. ",

    "THE INTERMEDIATE RUNG IS REAL AND MUST NOT BE REPORTED AS THE CEILING. A lens reading stored captures and refusing a row whose wording is not a contiguous run within one element, or whose nearest preceding heading names another subject, reaches MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE and stops there, because the wording and the capture both stay writable and safety depends on that lens executing and staying enrolled. It is the correct next step and it is one rung short of the derivation above. ",

    "WHY THIS RANKS RATHER THAN WAITS: the rows this class corrupts are consumed by cabinet-density screening, so a fused or foreign figure does not produce a visible error -- it produces a SITE THAT LOOKS LIKE A CANDIDATE. The audit that found these withdrew a metro from four readable densities to two and a corridor from two to one of twenty-eight, so the population the defect inflates is the population a planner would act on, and the corrected population is small enough that one bad row moves the conclusion. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
